#: ../../source/developer-guide/contributing.md:1
msgid "Contributing"
msgstr "参与贡献"

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contributing.md:3
msgid ""
"**Workflow**: branch from `main` → make your change → open a pull request "
"into `main` → get it reviewed if the change warrants it → merge. For a docs "
"change, `make -C docs strict` locally is the same check CI runs, so a local "
"pass means CI will pass too — see [Working on the "
"documentation](documentation.md)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contributing.md:9
msgid ""
"**Branch naming**: short and descriptive, e.g. `fix-cnetml-options-page` or "
"`add-slurm-tutorial`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contributing.md:27
msgid ""
"Then open a pull request into `main` on GitHub (a GUI git client works just "
"as well for these steps)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/contributing.md:30
msgid ""
"There's no issue tracker linked to branches/PRs yet — for now, just branch "
"and go."
msgstr ""

